## Review

- **Fix worth doing now — Medium:** `workspace_root` is not a stable hit-shape field. `HistorySearchHit` omits it when `None` (`crates/ocean-agent/src/lib.rs:92-95`), while legacy sessions deserialize without a workspace root (`crates/ocean-agent/src/session/mod.rs:5-15`) and search forwards that `None` (`crates/ocean-agent/src/session/mod.rs:577-585`). The daemon test only exercises a newly bound session and asserts the field exists (`crates/ocean-daemon/src/main.rs:18582-18595`). Serialize `null` consistently or explicitly test/document omission before establishing the new API contract.
- **Fix worth doing now — Medium:** The result limit does not bound search work. Every request reads and deserializes every session into memory (`crates/ocean-agent/src/session/mod.rs:522-562`), accumulates every matching message, then sorts all hits before truncation (`crates/ocean-agent/src/session/mod.rs:564-602`). Exact matching can additionally perform query-length comparisons across the transcript (`crates/ocean-agent/src/session/mod.rs:665-673`). Each request launches an unconstrained `spawn_blocking` scan (`crates/ocean-daemon/src/history_search.rs:46-49`), with no query-length or concurrent-search cap. Concurrent/typeahead requests could cause substantial I/O, CPU, and memory pressure. Add a query-size ceiling and bounded concurrency; bounding top-hit storage would also reduce amplification.
- **Correct:** No blocker found in privacy filtering, deterministic ranking/tie-breaking, malformed-file tolerance, Unicode-safe character-indexed excerpts, async executor isolation, or 1–50 result clamping. Tool-result text is excluded at `crates/ocean-agent/src/session/mod.rs:567-575`, and focused tests pass.
- **Note:** Requested `plan.md` and `progress.md` were absent. No files were modified, and unrelated TUI changes were preserved.

